CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc_node(sizeof(*buf)...) over kzalloc_node(sizeof(struct cs_etr_buffers)...)
#109: FILE: drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-tmc-etr.c:271:
+	buf = kzalloc_node(sizeof(struct cs_etr_buffers), GFP_KERNEL, node);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

